WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.363
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:28.633 --> 00:30.051
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

3
00:46.651 --> 00:47.819
You reek of alcohol.

4
00:48.403 --> 00:49.988
I'm sorry.

5
01:15.805 --> 01:16.806
Get off me.

6
01:22.437 --> 01:26.566
I swear, it was so dark in here I couldn't see a thing.

7
01:26.649 --> 01:28.443
Besides, I'm really drunk right now.

8
01:28.526 --> 01:29.611
Enough. Just get out.

9
01:29.694 --> 01:30.737
Okay.

10
01:32.864 --> 01:35.658
-Don't you need a hand getting up-- -I said get out!

11
01:41.748 --> 01:44.209
Well, that sobered me up.

12
01:48.630 --> 01:50.089
Damn it.

13
01:54.969 --> 01:55.803
Huh?

14
02:18.034 --> 02:19.035
Why is this…

15
02:24.791 --> 02:25.667
Mr. Baek.

16
02:28.586 --> 02:29.462
Sir.

17
02:32.298 --> 02:33.132
Sir…

18
02:37.178 --> 02:38.263
Sir.

19
02:41.140 --> 02:42.183
Ms. Na.

20
02:42.767 --> 02:43.726
Why is she here?

21
02:45.770 --> 02:47.313
Ms. Na.

22
02:49.315 --> 02:51.150
She reeks of alcohol.

23
02:59.659 --> 03:00.910
Ms. Na.

24
03:03.913 --> 03:05.331
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

25
03:05.415 --> 03:06.666
-What are you doing? -Ms…

26
03:09.377 --> 03:10.295
Sir.

27
03:13.423 --> 03:14.299
What's wrong?

28
03:17.844 --> 03:18.678
Are you hurt?

29
03:19.721 --> 03:23.224
The power went out yesterday, and I fell in the bathroom.

30
03:24.392 --> 03:28.604
That's why the digital locks on the gate and front door weren't working.

31
03:29.105 --> 03:29.939
Huh?

32
03:31.482 --> 03:33.735
-The digital locks are broken? -Yes.

33
03:38.740 --> 03:41.534
Why is that woman lying there?

34
03:42.160 --> 03:42.994
You didn't know?

35
03:45.496 --> 03:46.789
I'll wake her up now.

36
03:47.957 --> 03:48.875
Don't bother.

37
03:50.793 --> 03:51.627
Leave her alone.

38
04:14.859 --> 04:16.569
A power outage and broken locks.

39
04:18.571 --> 04:20.448
This doesn't seem like a coincidence.

40
04:20.531 --> 04:23.201
This has to be Choi Do-yoon's doing.

41
04:23.993 --> 04:25.203
Call a repairman first.

42
04:25.703 --> 04:26.871
Yes, sir.

43
04:28.081 --> 04:29.791
May I ask why Ms. Na is…

44
04:29.874 --> 04:31.250
Huh? What?

45
04:31.334 --> 04:34.128
What about her? Nothing happened between us yesterday.

46
04:34.212 --> 04:36.214
-Pardon? -What?

47
04:37.340 --> 04:38.174
Nothing, sir.

48
04:38.925 --> 04:39.759
Never mind.

49
04:41.719 --> 04:43.471
Shouldn't you see a doctor first?

50
04:43.554 --> 04:47.058
I just twisted it a little.

51
04:47.141 --> 04:49.435
It's much better than it was yesterday.

52
04:49.519 --> 04:50.353
I see.

53
04:51.354 --> 04:53.940
I'll get the locks fixed before your family arrives.

54
04:55.274 --> 04:57.485
-They're coming? -Did you forget?

55
04:57.568 --> 05:00.196
Your family's coming to celebrate your birthday.

56
05:04.492 --> 05:05.368
Right.

57
05:05.868 --> 05:09.122
I'm worried you hit your head when you fell yesterday.

58
05:09.205 --> 05:10.289
What are you doing?

59
05:10.373 --> 05:11.290
Your head--

60
05:12.959 --> 05:16.170
I'll be inside. Come in when you're done here.

61
05:36.732 --> 05:38.818
I'm sorry.

62
05:47.410 --> 05:48.494
Hello.

63
05:50.246 --> 05:54.750
You slept on the couch last night. I guess you were pretty drunk.

64
05:55.501 --> 05:58.963
Yeah, I was so drunk I don't remember anything.

65
05:59.046 --> 06:01.215
I woke up wondering why I was sleeping there.

66
06:14.812 --> 06:15.646
Gosh.

67
06:15.730 --> 06:17.940
Your chest is limping. Are you okay?

68
06:18.024 --> 06:19.150
Yeah, I'm…

69
06:21.944 --> 06:23.362
-"Chest"? -What?

70
06:23.446 --> 06:26.282
You just said my chest is limping.

71
06:27.700 --> 06:28.618
Your ankle.

72
06:28.701 --> 06:32.079
I asked if your ankle was okay. Ankle.

73
06:35.875 --> 06:38.085
Yeah, it's just a bit swollen.

74
06:38.169 --> 06:39.253
That's a relief.

75
06:39.754 --> 06:40.588
Yeah.

76
06:40.671 --> 06:43.758
I guess I'll have some breakfast.

77
06:49.263 --> 06:52.350
You should eat out. My family will be here soon.

78
06:53.017 --> 06:54.227
Your family? Why?

79
06:54.977 --> 06:56.437
It's my birthday today.

80
06:58.105 --> 06:59.190
Your birthday?

81
06:59.273 --> 07:00.983
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

82
07:01.067 --> 07:03.361
Well, why should I tell you?

83
07:03.444 --> 07:05.154
That's no way to spend a birthday.

84
07:05.238 --> 07:08.449
If I'd known it was your birthday, I could've gotten you a little something.

85
07:09.909 --> 07:11.786
I don't need a gift from you.

86
07:12.370 --> 07:14.664
Did you really have to put it like that?

87
07:15.581 --> 07:18.543
Fine. If you don't need one, I won't bother.

88
07:19.794 --> 07:20.753
Wait.

89
07:32.265 --> 07:33.182
Your chest…

90
07:37.186 --> 07:38.312
I'm sorry.

91
07:38.396 --> 07:41.899
I was just going to tell you to take off the rubber glove.

92
07:42.692 --> 07:43.859
You were just so light.

93
07:43.943 --> 07:47.738
It's just that I have no core strength. Yeah, I should take this off.

94
07:48.322 --> 07:49.156
Wow.

95
07:50.908 --> 07:52.034
What am I looking at?

96
07:52.118 --> 07:53.661
How did you even get…

97
07:55.454 --> 07:57.498
Gotta lock those doors, Ho-rang.

98
07:57.582 --> 08:00.876
Or bad guys like me will just walk right in.

99
08:03.629 --> 08:04.630
Girlfriend?

100
08:05.172 --> 08:06.090
Doesn't look like it.

101
08:06.173 --> 08:07.508
A one-night stand?

102
08:08.009 --> 08:09.510
Probably a bit low-rent.

103
08:09.594 --> 08:11.762
-Hey, Choi Do-yoon. -I'm his secretary.

104
08:12.763 --> 08:14.265
-Secretary? -Yes.

105
08:14.849 --> 08:15.850
Mr. Baek…

106
08:15.933 --> 08:18.352
Our senior managing director got hurt yesterday,

107
08:18.436 --> 08:20.313
so I came by on my day off.

108
08:20.855 --> 08:22.690
He got hurt? How?

109
08:22.773 --> 08:25.109
There was a power outage here yesterday.

110
08:25.192 --> 08:27.320
He could've been seriously hurt.

111
08:27.403 --> 08:29.405
Well, I'll be on my way.

112
08:29.488 --> 08:31.824
Happy birthday, sir.

113
08:50.509 --> 08:51.844
Wait.

114
08:52.678 --> 08:54.347
I should've brought my laptop.

115
08:55.389 --> 08:56.932
Oh, shoot.

116
09:27.171 --> 09:29.423
I guess you weren't hurt that badly.

117
09:31.467 --> 09:33.302
I'm sure you've been hoping I'd die.

118
09:33.386 --> 09:34.970
Sorry for being perfectly fine.

119
09:35.054 --> 09:37.264
How can you say something so horrible?

120
09:37.348 --> 09:40.810
Horrible? I thought you, of all people, would be unfazed.

121
09:41.811 --> 09:42.937
What does that mean?

122
09:43.646 --> 09:45.773
You can't possibly have forgotten.

123
09:46.357 --> 09:47.441
Or can you?

124
10:06.919 --> 10:08.170
Hello.

125
10:08.254 --> 10:09.922
Why are you limping?

126
10:10.005 --> 10:11.257
I just twisted my ankle.

127
10:11.757 --> 10:13.634
Did you know your lock's broken?

128
10:14.135 --> 10:17.430
Don't you know people like us have to keep security tight?

129
10:17.513 --> 10:20.683
I'm getting it fixed today. Thanks for your concern, Aunt.

130
10:22.393 --> 10:23.936
It shows a lack of competence.

131
10:44.331 --> 10:46.083
Damn it.

132
11:07.104 --> 11:09.190
Oh no. Are you okay, Ms. Secretary?

133
11:11.066 --> 11:12.651
I wonder why you're eating ramyeon

134
11:12.735 --> 11:16.113
at the convenience store outside Ho-rang's house instead of going home.

135
11:16.197 --> 11:17.740
I'm really curious.

136
11:17.823 --> 11:20.117
I was starving after working so hard.

137
11:20.201 --> 11:21.744
Cut the nonsense.

138
11:22.578 --> 11:25.998
You're not really his secretary. You two have something going on, right?

139
11:26.081 --> 11:26.916
Sorry?

140
11:26.999 --> 11:29.710
To celebrate his birthday, did you two…

141
11:30.586 --> 11:31.587
hook up?

142
11:32.838 --> 11:35.758
What's wrong? Did I hit a little too close to home?

143
11:36.592 --> 11:39.929
Baek Ho-rang has unexpected taste. Going for something like this.

144
11:40.888 --> 11:41.931
"Something like this"?

145
11:42.014 --> 11:44.058
So you've got some pride in you, huh?

146
11:44.141 --> 11:45.684
I guess that's kind of cute.

147
11:46.977 --> 11:47.978
How about

148
11:48.938 --> 11:51.106
you go out with me?

149
11:51.190 --> 11:53.692
I can do better than that clueless idiot.

150
11:57.112 --> 11:59.907
-Excuse me, Mr. Baek Ho-rang's cousin. -Yeah?

151
12:00.574 --> 12:03.285
Just call me Choi Do-yoon.

152
12:03.369 --> 12:06.622
Look at you giving your name without a shred of shame.

153
12:16.841 --> 12:18.676
I've lost my appetite. I'm done eating.

154
12:18.759 --> 12:21.303
Smells like burning trash in here.

155
12:21.804 --> 12:23.264
Damn it.

156
12:24.932 --> 12:26.016
What the hell?

157
12:26.851 --> 12:28.018
What was that? Seriously.

158
12:31.564 --> 12:34.650
Are you really turning this down? You'd be the face of TS.

159
12:35.150 --> 12:37.945
This is a huge opportunity, Eun-ho.

160
12:38.028 --> 12:40.614
Hanlim is involved in this TS project too.

161
12:40.698 --> 12:42.283
We're planning your US debut.

162
12:42.366 --> 12:45.619
Becoming the face of TS Resort would be a huge boost.

163
12:45.703 --> 12:48.539
How long are you going to stick to PSAs and charity ads?

164
12:48.622 --> 12:51.000
I want to make a positive impact as an actor.

165
12:51.834 --> 12:55.546
What's the point of being successful if I can't choose my projects?

166
12:55.629 --> 12:59.049
It was never about fame or money. You know that.

167
12:59.133 --> 13:03.429
That's our point. To do more projects, you need this kind of exposure.

168
13:03.512 --> 13:05.097
It's a positive cycle.

169
13:05.180 --> 13:06.891
More success, more impact.

170
13:06.974 --> 13:09.226
He's right, Eun-ho. Let's do the ad.

171
13:09.310 --> 13:13.564
You're only promoting your movie and reviewing scripts, so you have time.

172
13:20.237 --> 13:22.281
Let me decide after I see the concept.

173
13:27.494 --> 13:29.663
Why did you bring so much food?

174
13:29.747 --> 13:32.458
Eating well and taking care of yourself is a skill too.

175
13:32.541 --> 13:33.792
Just eat.

176
13:34.418 --> 13:36.962
I eat well. I have a housekeeper.

177
13:37.046 --> 13:39.423
This galbijjim came from Dojaewon early this morning.

178
13:39.506 --> 13:42.176
This one came from our hotel early this morning too.

179
13:42.259 --> 13:44.178
Nothing like your housekeeper's cooking.

180
13:44.762 --> 13:46.013
Have some tact.

181
13:46.096 --> 13:48.015
Thanks for looking out for me, Aunt.

182
13:50.434 --> 13:53.145
Just look at that smug grin. You brat.

183
13:53.729 --> 13:56.148
Mom, he's doing it on purpose.

184
13:56.649 --> 13:59.318
You don't have to bring food from TS Hotel.

185
13:59.902 --> 14:02.529
I hear it's been tough there lately.

186
14:06.075 --> 14:09.203
What's wrong with our hotel? Isn't TS Resort the one struggling?

187
14:09.286 --> 14:11.664
No, I heard the hotel's F&amp;B side is…

188
14:14.333 --> 14:16.502
already swamped.

189
14:17.044 --> 14:20.047
I feel bad increasing their workload for my birthday.

190
14:20.130 --> 14:21.590
Anything going on at the hotel?

191
14:21.674 --> 14:22.508
Huh?

192
14:23.968 --> 14:26.178
Of course not. Why would there be?

193
14:26.971 --> 14:28.263
It's the same as always.

194
14:28.931 --> 14:32.309
Isn't the hotel busy preparing for the 30th anniversary?

195
14:33.018 --> 14:33.852
Oh, that?

196
14:34.478 --> 14:35.396
Right, of course.

197
14:35.479 --> 14:38.190
Yeah, we're busy, but…

198
14:38.732 --> 14:39.942
What is wrong with you?

199
14:40.025 --> 14:41.193
Let me get that.

200
14:41.276 --> 14:43.070
Hey, get me a spoon!

201
14:44.697 --> 14:48.575
Do-yoon, why is your hand so red? Oh my, you're shaking too.

202
14:48.659 --> 14:51.328
I guess I have a bit of a tremor from exhaustion lately.

203
14:51.412 --> 14:54.164
-It's nothing. -You're shaking like you got electrocuted.

204
14:54.248 --> 14:55.499
I'm fine.

205
14:55.582 --> 14:56.667
Go ahead and eat.

206
14:57.543 --> 14:58.377
Ho-rang.

207
14:58.460 --> 14:59.586
Yes, Grandma.

208
15:00.170 --> 15:02.798
-I invited a guest over. -A guest?

209
15:23.318 --> 15:25.237
I think we got them, ma'am.

210
15:25.821 --> 15:28.115
That looks good. Thank you. I'm counting on you.

211
15:28.198 --> 15:31.076
I'll pick the photos and get back to you.

212
15:34.121 --> 15:36.415
Wow. Is she a celebrity?

213
15:39.084 --> 15:40.294
Or a chaebol?

214
15:41.211 --> 15:42.629
She's so pretty.

215
15:52.514 --> 15:54.600
There's been talk of you two getting married.

216
15:54.683 --> 15:57.936
I thought it'd be nice if she joined us, so I invited her.

217
15:58.604 --> 16:00.355
Happy birthday, Mr. Baek.

218
16:00.856 --> 16:02.441
-Oh. -Here's your present.

219
16:02.524 --> 16:03.859
Thank you.

220
16:03.942 --> 16:05.778
Seol-hee, you get prettier every day.

221
16:05.861 --> 16:08.363
You look like a model, not someone from an ad agency.

222
16:08.447 --> 16:09.406
Very gorgeous.

223
16:10.074 --> 16:12.868
Hanlim Advertising Company seems pretty solid lately.

224
16:13.452 --> 16:16.497
Everyone around me lights up when Hanlim's stock is mentioned.

225
16:17.998 --> 16:20.876
You two are close, right? You should sit facing each other.

226
16:20.959 --> 16:22.711
-Good idea. -Let him sit there.

227
16:22.795 --> 16:23.879
It's fine.

228
16:27.841 --> 16:29.176
Let's eat.

229
16:31.595 --> 16:32.721
Thank you for the meal.

230
16:51.615 --> 16:55.953
If I had my laptop with me, I could've gotten some writing done.

231
17:00.666 --> 17:03.585
Maybe I'll just read a web novel.

232
17:05.254 --> 17:06.088
Huh?

233
17:06.588 --> 17:08.966
Hey, this is the chaebol you're charging, right?

234
17:09.049 --> 17:09.883
Huh?

235
17:10.843 --> 17:12.010
"Baek Ho-rang"?

236
17:13.053 --> 17:15.514
BAEK HO-RANG AND HAN SEOL-HEE ANNOUNCE ENGAGEMENT

237
17:25.941 --> 17:27.943
Did you have to do this today of all days?

238
17:28.026 --> 17:30.988
Talks of your marriage have been ongoing for years.

239
17:31.071 --> 17:33.699
Even so, you announced it without consulting me.

240
17:33.782 --> 17:35.159
That's what I'm saying.

241
17:35.242 --> 17:36.869
This isn't right, Mom!

242
17:36.952 --> 17:39.496
A third-gen chaebol marriage announcement

243
17:39.580 --> 17:43.458
is basically a PR move to announce Ho-rang will inherit TS!

244
17:44.042 --> 17:45.335
You know that, Mom!

245
17:48.130 --> 17:50.799
Mother, in this day and age,

246
17:50.883 --> 17:53.719
you can't force Ho-rang into a marriage he doesn't want.

247
17:53.802 --> 17:56.013
I mean, Ho-rang's already quite sensitive.

248
17:56.096 --> 17:58.557
Look at him. He hurt his ankle.

249
17:58.640 --> 18:01.059
All because he didn't have someone there for him.

250
18:01.143 --> 18:03.312
It's a good thing it was just his ankle.

251
18:03.395 --> 18:05.105
It could've been worse.

252
18:05.189 --> 18:08.442
-It was just a coincidence-- -So was your mom and dad's accident.

253
18:16.033 --> 18:18.869
You never know when or how someone might go down.

254
18:18.952 --> 18:22.331
The more people you have around to cover your weaknesses,

255
18:22.414 --> 18:24.875
the more chess pieces you have to back you up,

256
18:25.626 --> 18:27.336
the better off you'll be.

257
18:29.379 --> 18:32.257
I know what's good for me. I'll decide for myself.

258
18:32.841 --> 18:34.509
-Stop being so stubborn. -No.

259
18:34.593 --> 18:36.428
You should stop being stubborn, Grandma.

260
18:38.722 --> 18:39.973
I'll issue a correction.

261
18:40.891 --> 18:42.434
You should go home now.

262
18:46.647 --> 18:48.273
Take down all the articles

263
18:48.357 --> 18:52.527
and issue a correction saying I will never marry Director Han.

264
18:54.655 --> 18:55.781
Sir.

265
18:57.074 --> 18:58.242
I think you should see this.

266
18:59.952 --> 19:02.329
The engagement article is getting positive reactions.

267
19:02.412 --> 19:05.249
The stock price, which had been falling, is now rebounding.

268
19:06.667 --> 19:08.168
Should we issue a correction?

269
19:09.503 --> 19:12.631
Think like Senior Managing Director Baek, not Baek Ho-rang.

270
19:12.714 --> 19:14.174
What would you do?

271
19:16.260 --> 19:17.094
Grandma.

272
19:17.177 --> 19:20.681
Seol-hee aside, if you marry into the Hanlim family,

273
19:20.764 --> 19:23.517
it'll be much easier for TS Resort and TS Hotel

274
19:23.600 --> 19:26.728
to enter overseas markets.

275
19:26.812 --> 19:28.772
I'm already working on expanding overseas.

276
19:29.481 --> 19:30.482
Please.

277
19:32.317 --> 19:34.778
Can't you respect my wishes just this once?

278
19:34.861 --> 19:37.990
If you can think and act more strategically than I can,

279
19:38.073 --> 19:39.324
then by all means.

280
19:39.408 --> 19:43.161
Were you like this with my parents too? Right up to the accident?

281
19:46.290 --> 19:48.542
I didn't have to push them.

282
19:48.625 --> 19:50.419
They did it all on their own.

283
19:54.298 --> 19:55.924
Marry Seol-hee.

284
20:08.395 --> 20:10.522
Sir, about the articles…

285
20:11.064 --> 20:11.982
Leave them.

286
20:12.774 --> 20:13.650
Then…

287
20:14.818 --> 20:17.279
I'll just have to do Hanlim's part too, right?

288
20:26.621 --> 20:28.332
This is exhausting, Mom.

289
20:28.415 --> 20:30.334
Ho-rang's not a kid anymore.

290
20:30.417 --> 20:33.879
How long will you keep serving him lavish meals like a VIP?

291
20:33.962 --> 20:36.423
She's right, Mother. It's a lot of work for you.

292
20:36.506 --> 20:39.092
Next time, let's just eat out or get him a gift--

293
20:39.176 --> 20:41.636
If you don't want to come, don't bother coming.

294
20:41.720 --> 20:44.639
Mom, I was just worried about you.

295
20:44.723 --> 20:46.391
Come on, you're hurting my feelings.

296
21:07.579 --> 21:08.872
Mr. Kim!

297
21:09.498 --> 21:10.832
You were here?

298
21:28.308 --> 21:29.643
PORTABLE CHARGER

299
21:35.816 --> 21:38.485
The person you're calling is unavailable.

300
22:13.061 --> 22:16.273
How long is she going to stay out? Jeez.

301
22:37.711 --> 22:38.587
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

302
22:45.635 --> 22:46.720
What are you doing?

303
22:46.803 --> 22:48.763
Why weren't you answering? Where were you?

304
22:48.847 --> 22:52.100
I guess I didn't notice. It was in my back pocket.

305
22:53.226 --> 22:55.687
Why are you so mad? Were you waiting for me?

306
22:55.770 --> 22:56.855
Waiting for you? As if.

307
22:58.231 --> 23:00.192
It was late, and I couldn't reach you, so…

308
23:00.942 --> 23:02.110
The battery!

309
23:02.611 --> 23:05.363
I need to charge my heart battery.

310
23:06.615 --> 23:10.577
I walked around the neighborhood for hours because of you.

311
23:12.078 --> 23:14.206
My family left after lunch.

312
23:14.831 --> 23:16.249
They did?

313
23:16.750 --> 23:19.419
My family spends all day together on birthdays.

314
23:20.212 --> 23:21.671
I should've come earlier, then.

315
23:21.755 --> 23:24.841
Anyway, I need to charge my battery, so let's go in.

316
23:28.762 --> 23:29.804
Mr. Baek!

317
23:29.888 --> 23:30.847
What is it?

318
23:30.931 --> 23:32.766
Hey, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

319
23:36.228 --> 23:37.646
Ta-da!

320
23:40.941 --> 23:44.194
It's your birthday. We can't just let it pass.

321
23:44.778 --> 23:46.821
I'll sing for you, so make a wish.

322
23:47.989 --> 23:50.951
Here's a special song selected just for you.

323
23:55.413 --> 23:58.708
It's Ho-rang the tiger's birthday

324
23:59.292 --> 24:02.921
The brave hero of the mountains

325
24:03.004 --> 24:06.174
-All the animals gather in the park -All the animals gather in the park

326
24:06.258 --> 24:09.219
And the grand ball begins

327
24:09.302 --> 24:12.764
The rabbit dances

328
24:12.847 --> 24:15.976
And the fox plays the violin

329
24:16.059 --> 24:19.187
Skippy-skip

330
24:19.271 --> 24:23.191
Skippy-skipping around

331
24:25.151 --> 24:26.236
Did you make a wish?

332
24:26.820 --> 24:28.947
Go on. Blow out the candle and make a wish.

333
24:34.703 --> 24:36.079
Happy birthday.

334
24:39.457 --> 24:40.333
Why…

335
24:43.295 --> 24:44.296
Why that song?

336
24:45.797 --> 24:49.259
Well, it's the first song I think of when I hear your name.

337
24:54.431 --> 24:57.684
What's this? Why do you look so shocked and moved?

338
24:59.060 --> 25:03.231
Did I just become the heroine who brought back

339
25:04.024 --> 25:06.109
your happy childhood memories?

340
25:10.905 --> 25:12.699
I think it's raining.

341
25:12.782 --> 25:14.075
Come on. Let's go eat cake.

342
25:31.217 --> 25:32.927
I read that article.

343
25:35.972 --> 25:37.098
That's…

344
25:37.182 --> 25:39.559
Is it one of those arranged chaebol marriages?

345
25:40.602 --> 25:43.480
You said you had no one else and you'd help me with romance.

346
25:43.563 --> 25:46.191
Isn't this a breach of contract?

347
25:46.858 --> 25:47.859
No, it's not.

348
25:48.485 --> 25:50.153
That article was my grandmother's doing,

349
25:51.237 --> 25:53.490
and that marriage isn't happening.

350
25:53.573 --> 25:55.450
We'll issue a correction in due course.

351
25:56.326 --> 25:57.661
I see.

352
25:58.912 --> 26:00.288
I mean it.

353
26:00.789 --> 26:02.332
My grandmother is…

354
26:05.502 --> 26:07.253
She can be a bit overbearing.

355
26:08.296 --> 26:09.964
I'll take care of it.

356
26:10.465 --> 26:12.759
Don't believe anything you hear about me getting married.

357
26:15.720 --> 26:18.723
Did your grandmother name you Baek Ho-rang?

358
26:23.603 --> 26:24.479
No.

359
26:25.063 --> 26:26.147
My parents did.

360
26:27.816 --> 26:29.567
Why did they name you Ho-rang?

361
26:31.236 --> 26:33.905
My father dreamed of a white tiger before I was born.

362
26:34.406 --> 26:37.283
The white tiger, the baekho, was in my mother's arms.

363
26:39.285 --> 26:42.247
That suits your surname perfectly. They gave you a great name.

364
26:45.375 --> 26:46.751
As for my birth dream,

365
26:47.252 --> 26:51.005
it was a tree with all kinds of fruit hanging from its branches.

366
26:51.089 --> 26:54.217
My mom said it looked so rare and special

367
26:54.300 --> 26:56.428
that she named me Bo-bae, meaning "precious."

368
26:57.470 --> 26:58.638
What a lovely dream.

369
27:00.306 --> 27:01.141
But

370
27:02.600 --> 27:03.643
why do you ask?

371
27:05.645 --> 27:07.272
To be honest,

372
27:07.355 --> 27:10.233
I think a birth dream is just a dream that seems special.

373
27:10.316 --> 27:13.194
I don't think they symbolize anything.

374
27:13.820 --> 27:16.072
But that's true love right there, isn't it?

375
27:16.656 --> 27:19.200
Giving your child the very best of everything,

376
27:19.284 --> 27:21.327
starting with your dream.

377
27:24.205 --> 27:26.541
So, happy birthday.

378
27:27.041 --> 27:30.420
Mr. Baek Ho-rang, whose parents gave him the gift of a white tiger dream.

379
27:36.217 --> 27:37.677
As for your grandma…

380
27:38.428 --> 27:40.722
I don't think she's overbearing for no reason.

381
27:40.805 --> 27:43.433
She's probably just looking out for you.

382
27:44.601 --> 27:47.187
She went about it the wrong way,

383
27:47.687 --> 27:49.773
but it comes from a place of love.

384
28:00.241 --> 28:01.451
When I was a kid,

385
28:02.619 --> 28:04.370
I lost my parents in an accident.

386
28:06.122 --> 28:08.958
They were on their way to see me when it happened.

387
28:09.959 --> 28:13.797
As soon as the press found out, they barged into my hospital room.

388
28:15.465 --> 28:17.801
Pushing cameras right in my face.

389
28:18.301 --> 28:22.555
Some paparazzi even dressed up as doctors or nurses to get in.

390
28:23.556 --> 28:24.891
So I get a little sensitive.

391
28:26.142 --> 28:27.811
Like yesterday, at the hospital.

392
28:29.062 --> 28:30.271
Situations like that.

393
28:32.482 --> 28:33.691
I didn't know.

394
28:44.118 --> 28:44.953
What was that?

395
28:46.037 --> 28:47.747
You've had it on you for a while.

396
28:54.629 --> 28:56.673
You should have told me.

397
28:56.756 --> 28:58.842
It's all in the past.

398
29:03.263 --> 29:04.514
Don't do it.

399
29:05.431 --> 29:06.975
Don't do what?

400
29:08.685 --> 29:11.604
You were about to comfort me, weren't you?

401
29:12.605 --> 29:16.192
It doesn't really resonate with me or comfort me, so don't.

402
29:18.361 --> 29:20.196
You're really cynical, aren't you?

403
29:20.989 --> 29:23.366
It's not like I was going to be rude.

404
29:23.449 --> 29:26.703
I was trying to comfort you, but you still didn't like it.

405
29:27.537 --> 29:32.792
I wasn't going to say anything that comforting anyway.

406
29:34.335 --> 29:36.379
But you looked at me so tenderly.

407
29:36.462 --> 29:40.258
I wasn't looking at you to comfort you.

408
29:40.341 --> 29:41.509
Then what?

409
30:08.953 --> 30:10.997
What's wrong with my heart?

410
31:02.340 --> 31:03.174
Oh, I…

411
31:03.257 --> 31:05.760
I'm getting tipsy. I should go to bed. Good night.

412
31:18.314 --> 31:20.692
Why is my heart beating so fast?

413
31:21.234 --> 31:23.194
My heart has never beaten this fast

414
31:23.277 --> 31:25.780
except when I electrocuted someone and knocked them out.

415
31:45.174 --> 31:48.219
Honestly, the mood was a little…

416
31:50.221 --> 31:51.764
something, wasn't it?

417
31:54.017 --> 31:57.228
It felt like we were about to kiss.

418
32:02.442 --> 32:03.735
This is it.

419
32:03.818 --> 32:05.236
Yes, this is it.

420
32:05.319 --> 32:06.696
I need to write this down!

421
32:47.945 --> 32:49.530
Is it broken?

422
33:08.382 --> 33:11.219
Your call can't be connected. Leave a message after the tone.

423
33:11.302 --> 33:12.929
SEOL-HEE

424
33:27.693 --> 33:28.736
Hey, it's me.

425
33:28.820 --> 33:31.364
That woman hanging around Baek Ho-rang.

426
33:35.326 --> 33:36.661
Is she really his secretary?

427
34:15.241 --> 34:19.829
These are all just distracting thoughts and worries.

428
35:11.088 --> 35:12.256
No.

429
35:42.370 --> 35:43.829
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

430
36:03.516 --> 36:04.892
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

431
36:50.813 --> 36:53.357
My gosh. What are you doing?

432
36:53.858 --> 36:54.775
You scared me.

433
36:56.235 --> 36:57.320
Well…

434
36:58.404 --> 37:01.324
It was time to charge, but you didn't come.

435
37:07.830 --> 37:09.790
But how did you get in here?

436
37:12.418 --> 37:13.919
Did you pick the lock?

437
37:14.003 --> 37:15.546
What do you take me for?

438
37:15.629 --> 37:17.715
The door was open!

439
37:17.798 --> 37:20.676
Even if it was open, why would you enter a woman's room?

440
37:20.760 --> 37:22.470
A woman's room? Please.

441
37:22.553 --> 37:23.554
This is my garage.

442
37:23.637 --> 37:25.931
And you are my portable charger under contract.

443
37:26.515 --> 37:28.434
Nothing more, nothing less.

444
37:30.186 --> 37:31.854
That woke me right up.

445
37:32.521 --> 37:33.731
Hey, excuse me?

446
37:33.814 --> 37:35.983
Who touches a portable charger's lips like…

447
37:39.487 --> 37:40.780
Like this?

448
37:40.863 --> 37:41.822
Who does that?

449
37:44.742 --> 37:46.452
That was…

450
37:47.787 --> 37:51.082
It was because you were biting your lips.

451
37:51.707 --> 37:53.084
And yesterday…

452
37:53.167 --> 37:54.835
Well…

453
37:55.336 --> 37:57.380
And yesterday, that secretary thing!

454
37:57.463 --> 37:58.297
Sorry?

455
37:58.381 --> 38:01.509
You told Choi Do-yoon you were my secretary.

456
38:04.303 --> 38:06.722
That freaking jerk of a cousin of yours?

457
38:06.806 --> 38:08.015
What about it?

458
38:08.599 --> 38:11.936
We have a contract, and this has to stay secret,

459
38:12.019 --> 38:13.562
so I had to think fast.

460
38:13.646 --> 38:16.399
Then use that quick thinking of yours to fix this mess!

461
38:18.025 --> 38:18.901
I…

462
38:19.735 --> 38:22.780
I came in here to say that.

463
38:22.863 --> 38:25.741
Are you telling me to pretend to be your secretary?

464
38:26.409 --> 38:30.037
I need to write a script. I don't even know what secretaries do.

465
38:30.121 --> 38:32.957
Just sit at your desk. You'll still get paid, of course.

466
38:33.040 --> 38:34.834
Forget the salary.

467
38:34.917 --> 38:37.211
I have a script to finish in three months.

468
38:37.294 --> 38:39.046
My future depends on it.

469
38:39.130 --> 38:41.048
Then write it during work hours.

470
38:42.341 --> 38:44.969
So I get paid, and I get to work on my script?

471
38:45.052 --> 38:47.805
If Choi Do-yoon finds out you lied about being my secretary,

472
38:47.888 --> 38:50.808
he'll do anything to dig up my weaknesses.

473
38:51.934 --> 38:53.269
You have no idea.

474
38:58.649 --> 38:59.567
Fine. I'll do it.

475
39:01.735 --> 39:02.570
Really?

476
39:02.653 --> 39:06.282
I'm the one who lied about being your secretary, after all.

477
39:09.869 --> 39:11.203
I'll be your secretary.

478
39:13.831 --> 39:14.665
All right.

479
39:15.749 --> 39:16.625
Then

480
39:17.835 --> 39:19.670
let's go to work together tomorrow.

481
39:22.298 --> 39:23.632
Okay, then.

482
39:23.716 --> 39:25.259
Morning charge now.

483
39:36.562 --> 39:39.482
That's just the sound it makes while charging.

484
39:39.565 --> 39:42.485
Yeah, sure. I have to go to the TV station today.

485
39:42.568 --> 39:46.280
I'll probably be back in the evening. It should last until then, right?

486
39:55.372 --> 39:56.957
Don't you have work to do?

487
39:57.041 --> 39:59.668
Are you going to keep following me? I'm here to work.

488
39:59.752 --> 40:00.669
Go do your thing.

489
40:00.753 --> 40:04.131
I'm just trying to stay close in case anything happens.

490
40:04.632 --> 40:06.467
I'll be at the café downstairs.

491
40:06.967 --> 40:09.678
Huh? You know there's a café here?

492
40:10.262 --> 40:11.514
Have you been here before?

493
40:14.683 --> 40:17.269
This is where we first met, remember?

494
40:18.187 --> 40:20.439
Oh. You're right.

495
40:20.523 --> 40:23.067
And this is where we had our first kiss.

496
40:25.903 --> 40:26.737
Well…

497
40:27.238 --> 40:29.615
I'll go get some work done.

498
40:29.698 --> 40:32.952
Go grab a coffee at the café downstairs or something.

499
40:53.305 --> 40:55.224
What do you think?

500
41:01.522 --> 41:02.356
Ms. Na.

501
41:03.857 --> 41:04.692
Yes?

502
41:05.859 --> 41:08.821
See? I knew you could do it.

503
41:09.488 --> 41:10.322
Is it okay?

504
41:10.406 --> 41:11.240
Bo-bae.

505
41:11.323 --> 41:13.742
This scene is super romantic. What's gotten into you?

506
41:13.826 --> 41:15.911
This is what I was talking about.

507
41:15.995 --> 41:17.788
A beer kiss? I love it!

508
41:17.871 --> 41:19.582
It's natural. It feels real.

509
41:19.665 --> 41:21.750
I had to stop and savor every word.

510
41:21.834 --> 41:24.712
My mouth is still watering, see? I can't make it stop.

511
41:25.296 --> 41:26.505
Pretty good, huh?

512
41:26.589 --> 41:29.258
Even as I was writing it, I knew I'd nailed it.

513
41:29.341 --> 41:30.884
Seriously, how did you do it?

514
41:30.968 --> 41:32.678
Are you seeing someone or what?

515
41:34.638 --> 41:36.015
-No. -She's not?

516
41:36.098 --> 41:37.099
Huh? No.

517
41:37.850 --> 41:38.934
Well, whatever.

518
41:39.018 --> 41:40.936
And this one. The Hangang River scene.

519
41:41.020 --> 41:43.689
It's a bit cliché, but I love it.

520
41:44.273 --> 41:46.900
"He got hurt for me, but he only cares if I'm okay."

521
41:46.984 --> 41:48.235
That's what I'm like!

522
41:50.070 --> 41:54.450
Bo-bae has been an expert on romance novels, movies, and comics

523
41:54.533 --> 41:56.201
since she was little.

524
41:56.285 --> 41:58.412
I guess it's finally paying off!

525
41:58.495 --> 42:02.124
Yeah, I think so too. She's got it. She's got the hang of it!

526
42:02.207 --> 42:05.628
You're right. I think I've got the hang of it.

527
42:05.711 --> 42:07.296
Keep this up, okay?

528
42:07.379 --> 42:10.674
Next episode, then the next, all the way to the finale. Okay?

529
42:10.758 --> 42:12.384
How about a dance, everyone?

530
42:12.885 --> 42:14.219
She's got the hang of it

531
42:14.303 --> 42:15.596
Got the hang of it, hey!

532
42:15.679 --> 42:17.473
Na Bo-bae's got the hang of it

533
42:17.556 --> 42:18.557
Hey!

534
42:19.266 --> 42:20.851
Today's meeting is important, okay?

535
42:20.934 --> 42:23.312
If this goes well, you'll make your Hollywood debut.

536
42:23.395 --> 42:25.439
I'm so nervous.

537
42:25.939 --> 42:27.775
Hey, no need to be nervous.

538
42:27.858 --> 42:29.610
You speak great English.

539
42:29.693 --> 42:31.528
You're ready for this, dude.

540
42:34.365 --> 42:35.199
One sec.

541
42:36.992 --> 42:38.410
Hello, Director.

542
42:38.494 --> 42:40.287
We're almost there.

543
42:41.622 --> 42:43.707
You mean right now?

544
42:45.584 --> 42:46.794
It's Bo-bae.

545
42:47.461 --> 42:48.295
Yes.

546
42:49.755 --> 42:52.299
Of course. Eun-ho's always ready.

547
42:53.676 --> 42:55.344
Every time I look away, that punk…

548
42:55.427 --> 42:58.222
Sorry? Oh, no, I wasn't talking to you, sir.

549
42:58.305 --> 42:59.682
Of course not.

550
43:01.350 --> 43:02.893
Sorry I kept you waiting.

551
43:02.976 --> 43:05.813
I got a lot of compliments today.

552
43:06.313 --> 43:09.149
Are you a kid? Getting excited over compliments?

553
43:15.239 --> 43:16.240
Bo-bae.

554
43:17.616 --> 43:19.535
Eun-ho. What are you doing here?

555
43:19.618 --> 43:20.911
Hello, Mr. Ji Eun-ho.

556
43:21.495 --> 43:22.454
Hello.

557
43:24.957 --> 43:27.710
I'm just here for a meeting. What are you doing here?

558
43:27.793 --> 43:31.046
I met with Director Yeom and Seo-jeong for feedback on the script.

559
43:32.798 --> 43:33.632
And this is?

560
43:34.591 --> 43:35.926
Oh, he's…

561
43:36.969 --> 43:38.762
just a friend.

562
43:39.972 --> 43:43.517
I didn't know you had a friend like him.

563
43:44.518 --> 43:47.813
He's a friend and a source. We met through work recently.

564
43:48.731 --> 43:50.941
Good to see you again. I'm Baek Ho-rang.

565
43:52.151 --> 43:54.862
Through work, Ms. Na Bo-bae and I

566
43:54.945 --> 43:57.489
have been getting pretty close recently.

567
43:58.949 --> 44:00.909
I'm sure you already know my name.

568
44:00.993 --> 44:03.245
I met Ms. Na when she made her debut,

569
44:03.328 --> 44:06.123
and we've been very close ever since.

570
44:15.132 --> 44:17.009
Did you two know each other?

571
44:17.885 --> 44:19.428
He's high up at TS Resort.

572
44:19.511 --> 44:21.722
Yeah, that's right.

573
44:23.724 --> 44:26.435
I got a secretary job at TS Resort for my research.

574
44:26.518 --> 44:28.145
For about three months.

575
44:28.228 --> 44:31.273
So I can't really call him my friend. He's my boss, really.

576
44:31.774 --> 44:34.568
Oh, your boss?

577
44:34.651 --> 44:36.862
Then you two are probably not that close.

578
44:36.945 --> 44:38.197
Not that close?

579
44:38.280 --> 44:40.282
Ms. Na and I

580
44:40.365 --> 44:42.493
have been stuck together like glue lately.

581
44:43.452 --> 44:46.622
That's what a secretary does, you know.

582
44:48.791 --> 44:50.375
It's great you're so dedicated,

583
44:50.459 --> 44:52.002
but take care of yourself too.

584
44:56.882 --> 44:59.676
You know I was the male lead in her debut show, right?

585
44:59.760 --> 45:03.263
Oh, that show. Wistful something, right?

586
45:03.347 --> 45:05.474
Yes, Wistful Youth.

587
45:05.557 --> 45:06.391
Did you watch it?

588
45:06.475 --> 45:08.310
No, not yet.

589
45:09.394 --> 45:11.688
You should watch it. It's a real masterpiece.

590
45:13.899 --> 45:17.903
I fell for her back then, and I've been following her ever since.

591
45:17.986 --> 45:20.155
Ms. Na here is a really good writer.

592
45:20.239 --> 45:22.074
Stop it, Eun-ho.

593
45:22.699 --> 45:24.076
What? It's true.

594
45:24.159 --> 45:26.912
If you ask me to be the lead, I'll come running.

595
45:26.995 --> 45:29.414
If you want to be the lead, I'd totally--

596
45:29.498 --> 45:32.751
A big star like you must be busy. We shouldn't keep you.

597
45:32.835 --> 45:36.129
I'll be in touch soon.

598
45:42.052 --> 45:43.554
What? Why is he leaving alone?

599
45:44.304 --> 45:47.474
Well, I'll call you later, Eun-ho.

600
45:47.558 --> 45:48.392
Bye.

601
45:48.892 --> 45:50.686
Hey, why are you leaving alone?

602
46:06.702 --> 46:08.328
Well done. You all worked so hard.

603
46:08.412 --> 46:10.080
-I'm good. -Well done. Great work!

604
46:10.163 --> 46:12.916
Our show's called Wistful Youth,

605
46:13.417 --> 46:15.586
but our ratings will be anything but wistful!

606
46:15.669 --> 46:16.837
Anything but wistful!

607
46:17.588 --> 46:20.424
-Anything but wistful! -Anything but wistful!

608
46:20.507 --> 46:21.341
Wistful!

609
46:21.425 --> 46:23.594
Youth!

610
46:23.677 --> 46:25.429
Great work, team!

611
46:25.512 --> 46:26.680
Great work!

612
46:26.763 --> 46:28.974
Huh? Where's Ms. Na?

613
46:29.057 --> 46:31.393
-She's outside. I'll get her. -She should be here.

614
46:31.476 --> 46:32.436
Yes.

615
46:32.519 --> 46:33.687
Have a seat, sir!

616
46:33.770 --> 46:35.022
-Seo-jeong! -Yes, sir!

617
46:35.105 --> 46:36.398
You did great.

618
46:36.481 --> 46:38.025
-Me? Really? -Yeah.

619
46:38.108 --> 46:38.984
Ms. Na.

620
46:39.693 --> 46:40.903
Ms. Na, are you okay?

621
46:43.155 --> 46:45.657
The director is looking for you. Are you drunk?

622
46:58.003 --> 46:58.837
Ms. Na.

623
47:01.548 --> 47:05.761
If you think you're too drunk to remember this,

624
47:06.553 --> 47:08.055
can I tell you something?

625
47:11.516 --> 47:12.935
To tell you the truth,

626
47:13.727 --> 47:14.728
I've

627
47:15.228 --> 47:16.772
liked you since…

628
47:21.860 --> 47:22.945
That stings!

629
47:24.655 --> 47:25.489
Nope!

630
47:26.907 --> 47:29.242
What was that just now?

631
47:29.826 --> 47:31.328
Do you think it'll work out?

632
47:31.411 --> 47:35.332
Even the slightest touch from me zaps you.

633
47:35.832 --> 47:40.420
How can I date anyone?

634
47:53.976 --> 47:56.353
But what if someone still likes you?

635
47:59.189 --> 48:01.066
Is now really the time to date?

636
48:02.109 --> 48:04.778
Everyone's obsessed with dating.

637
48:04.861 --> 48:07.322
We should work!

638
48:07.406 --> 48:10.117
We should be successful first, you know?

639
48:10.617 --> 48:12.202
Once we're successful…

640
48:14.454 --> 48:15.747
can we date then?

641
48:15.831 --> 48:16.999
Of course.

642
48:17.082 --> 48:18.250
Really?

643
48:24.715 --> 48:26.466
They're probably not dating.

644
48:26.967 --> 48:28.844
She still has that power.

645
48:29.636 --> 48:32.305
So how is he okay?

646
48:33.223 --> 48:34.349
-What's going on? -Sorry.

647
48:34.433 --> 48:35.475
Hey, Ji Eun-ho!

648
48:36.393 --> 48:38.895
Why are you here? We're supposed to meet the director.

649
48:38.979 --> 48:40.105
Right.

650
48:40.188 --> 48:42.190
Please put your phones away. No photos.

651
48:42.274 --> 48:43.233
I'm sorry.

652
48:43.316 --> 48:45.360
Let's go. Get a hold of yourself.

653
48:46.028 --> 48:47.154
I'm sorry.

654
48:49.948 --> 48:53.744
Do you remember the last term you added to the contract?

655
48:56.955 --> 48:59.249
"Neither of us shall see anyone of the opposite gender"?

656
49:01.710 --> 49:02.919
You mean Eun-ho?

657
49:05.005 --> 49:07.382
Eun-ho is just a close friend.

658
49:07.883 --> 49:08.717
And my savior.

659
49:09.301 --> 49:10.302
Savior?

660
49:10.969 --> 49:14.389
Eun-ho was the only one who stopped me from quitting the drama.

661
49:14.473 --> 49:16.641
He said he loved my writing

662
49:17.267 --> 49:20.729
and would act in it himself to show everyone how amazing it was.

663
49:22.147 --> 49:23.732
He's such a cool fan, isn't he?

664
49:24.232 --> 49:26.318
Cool fan, my ass.

665
49:28.945 --> 49:31.073
Did Mr. Baek hire a new secretary?

666
49:37.829 --> 49:39.956
I've never seen her before.

667
50:06.191 --> 50:08.401
-Good morning. -Good morning, sir.

668
50:12.322 --> 50:15.700
This is my new personal secretary starting today.

669
50:15.784 --> 50:18.662
She'll be working directly for me.

670
50:18.745 --> 50:20.247
Don't give her any other work.

671
50:21.665 --> 50:22.791
Ms. Na.

672
50:24.501 --> 50:26.795
Hello. I'm Na Bo-bae.

673
50:26.878 --> 50:30.674
I'll be assisting Mr. Baek Ho-rang… I mean, the senior managing director.

674
50:30.757 --> 50:32.134
Nice to work with you all.

675
50:37.389 --> 50:41.518
I'm sure you've seen the articles about my engagement to Director Han.

676
50:41.601 --> 50:43.645
For now, don't respond to them.

677
50:43.728 --> 50:45.647
Just say it's confidential.

678
50:46.231 --> 50:49.109
So, are you really getting married, sir?

679
50:49.609 --> 50:52.988
When I say it's confidential, I mean it, Mr. Lee.

680
50:55.490 --> 50:57.868
That's all the executive office needs to know.

681
50:57.951 --> 50:59.327
Yes, sir. My apologies.

682
50:59.411 --> 51:00.996
Get Ms. Na a desk.

683
51:01.830 --> 51:02.664
Yes, sir.

684
51:02.747 --> 51:05.250
Let's make today count too.

685
51:06.251 --> 51:07.252
Let's do this.

686
51:24.477 --> 51:26.730
You're wearing gloves?

687
51:27.981 --> 51:29.232
Aren't they uncomfortable?

688
51:30.233 --> 51:32.485
Oh, these…

689
51:33.195 --> 51:36.781
I'm a bit germophobic.

690
51:36.865 --> 51:38.992
I see.

691
51:39.075 --> 51:42.287
A germophobic secretary?

692
51:43.371 --> 51:45.165
That won't be easy.

693
51:45.248 --> 51:47.292
Yes, sir. Got it.

694
51:48.168 --> 51:49.211
Ms. Na.

695
51:51.213 --> 51:52.505
Mr. Baek is asking for you.

696
51:53.798 --> 51:54.674
Me?

697
52:00.513 --> 52:01.556
What is it?

698
52:04.184 --> 52:05.602
What have you been doing?

699
52:06.853 --> 52:09.356
I was just about to write my script.

700
52:09.439 --> 52:10.857
You said I could write.

701
52:10.941 --> 52:12.692
You said you wouldn't make me work.

702
52:12.776 --> 52:17.113
But you should at least look like you're working.

703
52:26.581 --> 52:28.333
Please make a copy of this.

704
52:34.881 --> 52:36.258
Why are you wearing gloves?

705
52:36.341 --> 52:37.926
Mind your own business.

706
52:40.053 --> 52:43.682
Tell Ms. Na to bring me this week's report.

707
52:44.182 --> 52:47.060
Hey, ask Ms. Na if she knows how to make a PowerPoint.

708
52:47.560 --> 52:50.438
Hey, get me sparkling water from the break room.

709
52:50.522 --> 52:52.983
No, Ms. Na. Not you, Mr. Yoon.

710
53:10.000 --> 53:11.126
Sir.

711
53:14.170 --> 53:15.171
Yeah. Hey.

712
53:15.672 --> 53:16.506
Yeah.

713
53:17.340 --> 53:18.633
Is there something you need?

714
53:18.717 --> 53:20.135
Oh, just do your work.

715
53:20.218 --> 53:22.095
Sit down and get back to it.

716
53:25.598 --> 53:26.433
Ms. Na.

717
53:27.267 --> 53:30.812
We'll have to revise the schedule we put together earlier today.

718
53:34.024 --> 53:34.858
Pardon?

719
53:34.941 --> 53:36.318
The schedule.

720
53:36.401 --> 53:38.695
That we put together earlier today.

721
53:39.362 --> 53:41.197
Right.

722
53:41.823 --> 53:44.534
Yes. Go on, sir.

723
53:45.201 --> 53:46.953
What does your new schedule look like, sir?

724
53:47.579 --> 53:50.040
I'll be inspecting the resort shoot site at 1 p.m.,

725
53:50.123 --> 53:52.500
and I'll attend a meeting from 2 p.m. to 3 p.m.

726
53:52.584 --> 53:54.377
Then I'll receive a performance report

727
53:54.461 --> 53:56.880
from the lounge manager between 3 p.m. and 3:30 p.m.

728
53:56.963 --> 54:00.342
From 3:30 p.m. to 6 p.m., I'll be reviewing and approving reports.

729
54:00.425 --> 54:01.259
And at 6 p.m…

730
54:01.343 --> 54:03.553
Just quit your job and become a rapper.

731
54:03.636 --> 54:04.637
…leave work with me.

732
54:05.221 --> 54:07.265
You said I wouldn't have to work. For fuck's sake.

733
54:07.349 --> 54:08.767
Did you get all that?

734
54:08.850 --> 54:11.436
Yes, I wrote it down exactly.

735
54:18.485 --> 54:22.238
So, how's the rebranding project going?

736
54:22.322 --> 54:24.616
Our team is developing the concept.

737
54:24.699 --> 54:27.702
We plan to submit the draft by the end of this week.

738
54:28.703 --> 54:32.916
How's the target analysis and market research coming along?

739
54:33.583 --> 54:35.627
HE'S HEADING TO THE RESORT SHOOT SITE

740
54:50.850 --> 54:52.435
A NEW FEMALE SECRETARY HAS JOINED

741
54:52.519 --> 54:54.437
HE'S COMING IN AFTER A PERSONAL APPOINTMENT

742
54:54.521 --> 54:56.022
HE'LL EAT AT HOME WITH HIS FAMILY

743
55:09.202 --> 55:12.247
I think they're filming something here.

744
55:12.330 --> 55:14.958
This is our first time sponsoring a drama shoot location.

745
55:15.041 --> 55:16.209
A drama?

746
55:16.292 --> 55:18.086
Never been to a mini-series set, right?

747
55:19.003 --> 55:20.213
Take a good look.

748
55:20.839 --> 55:22.382
That's why I brought you here.

749
55:34.853 --> 55:38.231
I'll go talk to the person in charge. Wait here for a moment.

750
55:47.907 --> 55:49.617
Why is Director Yeom here?

751
55:50.118 --> 55:52.162
He thinks I'm busy working on the script.

752
55:54.664 --> 55:55.707
I'm sorry.

753
55:57.333 --> 55:58.209
Bo-bae.

754
55:58.918 --> 56:00.170
Ju-hee.

755
56:05.091 --> 56:06.092
What the…

756
56:07.051 --> 56:07.969
What?

757
56:09.095 --> 56:10.138
What the hell?

758
56:10.722 --> 56:11.931
When does filming start?

759
56:12.015 --> 56:13.016
Why are you here?

760
56:13.099 --> 56:16.769
This is my resort, so of course I should be here.

761
56:18.104 --> 56:21.065
But everyone seems so relaxed.

762
56:21.149 --> 56:23.943
Oh man. Don't you worry.

763
56:24.027 --> 56:26.905
We won't slack off or go over the schedule, sir.

764
56:26.988 --> 56:28.531
Go tell the actors to gather.

765
56:28.615 --> 56:30.366
Have them use the back gate.

766
56:30.450 --> 56:31.534
-Okay? -Got it.

767
56:32.827 --> 56:33.786
Who's that?

768
56:35.455 --> 56:36.539
Isn't that Ms. Na?

769
56:38.249 --> 56:39.584
Yeah, it is.

770
56:40.210 --> 56:41.419
She came with me.

771
56:42.003 --> 56:43.421
How do you know her?

772
56:44.088 --> 56:45.882
Right, you asked me about her the other day.

773
56:48.176 --> 56:49.427
What's with you two?

774
56:56.559 --> 56:58.811
Are you one of the guys lining up to date her?

775
57:00.063 --> 57:00.939
"Lining up"?

776
57:01.022 --> 57:02.649
She told me the other day.

777
57:02.732 --> 57:06.027
She said she was popular and had guys lining up to go out with her.

778
57:06.778 --> 57:08.112
I knew it.

779
57:08.196 --> 57:11.783
No wonder her script has been getting better recently.

780
57:15.537 --> 57:18.873
If Ms. Kang finds out about this, she's going to flip out.

781
57:19.582 --> 57:20.750
What are you doing here?

782
57:22.418 --> 57:23.753
Did Director Yeom call you?

783
57:25.713 --> 57:27.173
Well, I…

784
57:29.509 --> 57:30.593
I'm here for work.

785
57:32.303 --> 57:34.639
You work part-time at TS Resort?

786
57:35.473 --> 57:36.307
Well…

787
57:37.308 --> 57:38.226
Yeah.

788
57:38.309 --> 57:41.145
Didn't you work at a café before?

789
57:41.729 --> 57:44.148
You really work hard, Bo-bae.

790
57:44.232 --> 57:47.193
I'm so busy writing I don't have time to do anything else.

791
57:48.778 --> 57:50.446
Gosh, what's with that face?

792
57:50.947 --> 57:54.617
You're so intimidating. I can't even show that I care.

793
57:57.245 --> 57:58.079
Who's that?

794
57:58.663 --> 57:59.539
No way!

795
58:00.206 --> 58:02.625
Is that Baek Ho-rang?

796
58:03.459 --> 58:04.294
What?

797
58:04.377 --> 58:06.254
The guy next to Director Yeom.

798
58:06.754 --> 58:08.923
The one who's looking at me now.

799
58:09.007 --> 58:11.718
Ho-rang? What, like a tiger?

800
58:12.427 --> 58:14.095
That's a person's name?

801
58:17.932 --> 58:20.018
You don't even know the TS heir?

802
58:20.935 --> 58:23.855
You need to know their world too.

803
58:23.938 --> 58:25.356
You're a writer, after all.

804
58:25.440 --> 58:27.817
What Korean drama doesn't have a chaebol character?

805
58:28.818 --> 58:30.653
Oh, yeah. Right.

806
58:31.904 --> 58:33.197
Actually,

807
58:33.823 --> 58:35.116
there was a rumor

808
58:35.199 --> 58:37.827
that he stays out of the media because he's ugly.

809
58:38.745 --> 58:40.580
He could pass for an actor.

810
58:41.998 --> 58:44.417
There's something weird about their relationship.

811
58:44.500 --> 58:49.964
To be precise, Ms. Kang sees Ms. Na as a threat and doesn't like her.

812
58:50.632 --> 58:52.592
I thought they were close.

813
58:52.675 --> 58:53.926
Close, my ass.

814
58:54.010 --> 58:57.472
Ms. Kang is jealous of Ms. Na.

815
58:57.555 --> 58:59.515
She's doing much better than Ms. Na,

816
58:59.599 --> 59:02.727
but she always looks down on her in front of other people.

817
59:03.269 --> 59:04.937
I don't get why she's like that.

818
59:05.438 --> 59:07.774
He must be here to see me.

819
59:08.274 --> 59:09.776
I heard he's a fan of mine.

820
59:10.818 --> 59:11.653
Fan?

821
59:11.736 --> 59:14.906
I've written several shows, you know.

822
59:17.325 --> 59:20.370
Still, nothing beats having Ji Eun-ho as your fan

823
59:20.453 --> 59:22.538
and following you around.

824
59:22.622 --> 59:24.332
I need to work harder.

825
59:30.380 --> 59:31.589
Here he comes.

826
59:40.515 --> 59:43.101
I'm Baek Ho-rang, senior managing director at TS Resort.

827
59:43.768 --> 59:46.854
I'm Kang Ju-hee, the writer of this drama.

828
59:47.605 --> 59:48.690
Ms. Na.

829
59:50.024 --> 59:51.359
Do you like the resort?

830
59:53.569 --> 59:57.198
We at TS are interested in sponsoring your next show,

831
59:57.281 --> 59:59.450
so we've sent you several proposals.

832
01:00:00.410 --> 01:00:02.620
But you haven't given us an answer.

833
01:00:03.454 --> 01:00:06.624
That's why you came here with me today, right?

834
01:00:07.125 --> 01:00:08.167
To inspect the site.

835
01:00:10.128 --> 01:00:10.962
Pardon?

836
01:00:11.045 --> 01:00:13.506
Do you know Bo-bae?

837
01:00:13.589 --> 01:00:14.924
Of course I do.

838
01:00:15.425 --> 01:00:16.259
I am

839
01:00:17.260 --> 01:00:18.845
a huge fan

840
01:00:20.096 --> 01:00:21.806
of Ms. Na Bo-bae, you see.

841
01:02:08.996 --> 01:02:13.626
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
